<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-W.Australia in A$9 mln freight cut for grain.</title>
<headline>RTRS-W.Australia in A$9 mln freight cut for grain.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A drop in Western Australian grain freight rates to go into effect on October 1 will save the state's farmers about A$9 million this season, Transport Minister Eric Charlton said on Monday.</p>
<p>The new rail freight rate for grain has been reduced by 11.82 percent after inflation, offering farmers savings of more than A$9 million if the new crop exceeded last year's harvest, Charlton said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new grain freight rate was set as part of an annual review of a five-year contract drawn up in 1994 between the state rail authority Westrail and the grain industry.  </p>
<p>It ensures that productivity gains by Westrail are passed on to growers.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
